      "level": 1,
      "text": "5. Hexadecimal"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "b707d5c1-7bde-5f36-ae0f-6019b2b359a9",
      "citations": [],
      "text": "Binary numbers get long fast, so we use hex as shorthand. Hex is base 16, and $16 = 2^4$, so **one hex digit is exactly 4 bits**.\n\nHex needs 16 digits. After 9 it uses letters: A = 10, B = 11, C = 12, D = 13, E = 14, F = 15."
    },
