    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "28bf3b0b-67a6-5675-919f-8af9020ae8d9",
      "citations": [],
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Binary → hex: group by 4 from the point"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "id": "9706c0a6-4a7c-530b-878f-a9daeb4ef104",
      "citations": [],
      "ordered": true,
      "items": [
        "**Start at the point.** Group bits in fours going **left** for the whole part and **right** for the fraction.",
        "**Pad with zeros on the outside ends** if a group is short (far left, or far right).",
        "**Swap** each group of 4 for its hex digit."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "equation",
      "id": "151f9041-dcdb-596a-be75-9eb4fae464ae",
      "citations": [
        {
          "source_id": "ff6535b5-436e-42d5-8e1e-da0e01122696",
          "version": 1,
          "chunk_id": "7e86764a-353e-4b9a-9c2b-0aeaeabedf63"
        },
        {
          "source_id": "ff6535b5-436e-42d5-8e1e-da0e01122696",
          "version": 1,
          "chunk_id": "306c2d70-d7a0-4134-bb40-4d841072b4a5"
        }
      ],
      "latex": "(10110110.101)_2 \\;\\to\\; 1011\\;0110\\,.\\,1010 \\;\\to\\; (\\mathrm{B6.A})_{16}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "66690c66-45ff-5b9f-a0e2-9eed4788e6e0",
      "citations": [],
      "text": "Why pad on the outside? $.101$ and $.1010$ are the same number, just like $0.5 = 0.50$. Padding the inside, $.0101$, would change the value."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "54168a41-b483-5ebd-b9a5-27c31fe8c415",
      "citations": [],
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Hex → binary: swap each digit for 4 bits"
    },
    {
      "type": "equation",
      "id": "bbac496e-2775-5add-877b-72eb0dc641d7",
      "citations": [],
      "latex": "(2\\mathrm{F}.4)_{16} \\;\\to\\; 0010\\;1111\\,.\\,0100 \\;\\to\\; (101111.01)_2"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "f7f2fb5d-2cf9-5684-bce1-607ab82314ab",
      "citations": [],
      "text": "Drop the leading zeros on the left and the trailing zeros on the right at the end."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "30dd606f-c78b-5d18-983b-6d2ac34847c0",
      "citations": [],
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Hex → decimal: places are worth 16, 1, 1/16"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "d964e83b-55b0-551c-b271-f221ee1e964a",
      "citations": [],
      "text": "Same idea as binary, but each place is worth 16 times the one to its right."
    },
    {
      "type": "equation",
      "id": "26e1c705-8e8b-5f5f-b786-b5aeaee19fbd",
      "citations": [],
      "latex": "(2\\mathrm{F}.4)_{16} = 2(16) + 15(1) + \\tfrac{4}{16} = 32+15+0.25 = 47.25"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "f3c97e6f-53ed-51b0-8c40-ee050cef020f",
      "citations": [],
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Decimal → hex: go through binary"
    },
    {
      "type": "worked_example",
      "id": "972c95c0-f7ec-592a-a763-8deca1869b6b",
      "citations": [],
      "title": "Decimal to hex with a fraction",
      "prompt": "Convert $200.75$ to hexadecimal.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "explanation": "Whole part to binary. $200 = 128+64+8$.",
          "latex": "200=(11001000)_2"
        },
        {
          "explanation": "Fraction to binary: $0.75\\times2=1.5$ → 1, $0.5\\times2=1.0$ → 1.",
          "latex": "0.75=(.11)_2"
        },
        {
          "explanation": "Group by 4 from the point, padding the fraction on the right.",
          "latex": "1100\\;1000\\,.\\,1100"
        },
        {
          "explanation": "Swap each group for a hex digit.",
          "latex": "(\\mathrm{C8.C})_{16}"
        },
        {
          "explanation": "Check in decimal.",
          "latex": "12(16)+8+\\tfrac{12}{16}=200.75"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "$(\\mathrm{C8.C})_{16}$."
    },
    {
      "type": "practice_problem",
      "id": "bdf2cc72-0f37-5eab-8b44-d3df0aa53f7b",
      "citations": [],
      "title": "Try it: both directions",
      "prompt": "(a) Convert $(3\\mathrm{A}.8)_{16}$ to decimal and to binary. (b) Convert $45.25$ to hex.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "explanation": "(a) Decimal: A = 10 and the 8 sits in the 1/16 place.",
          "latex": "3(16)+10+\\tfrac8{16}=58.5"
        },
        {
          "explanation": "(a) Binary: swap each digit for 4 bits.",
          "latex": "0011\\;1010\\,.\\,1000\\to(111010.1)_2"
        },
        {
          "explanation": "(b) $45 = 32+8+4+1$ and $0.25 = .01$.",
          "latex": "45.25=(101101.01)_2"
        },
        {
          "explanation": "(b) Group by 4 from the point.",
          "latex": "0010\\;1101\\,.\\,0100\\to(\\mathrm{2D.4})_{16}"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "(a) $58.5$ and $(111010.1)_2$. (b) $(\\mathrm{2D.4})_{16}$.",
      "difficulty": "intermediate",
      "origin": "original"
    }
  ],
